notes=['Recovered the non-containment symbol and its direction, SoML^cc⊈PPA^cc.','Defined nonuniform families, exact deterministic local protocols, public fixed output labels, and the log|V|+maximum-local-communication cost.','Restored the source’s descending integer meter and all exceptional-vertex rules, including isolated PPA vertices.','Separated abstract protocol cost from an actual communication algorithm that searches the entire graph.','Checked the 2022 survey and 2024 query/oracle separation; the latter explicitly leaves communication analogues for further work.']
save(i,dict(
 title='SoML versus PPA in communication complexity',
 formal='Is SoMLᶜᶜ⊈PPAᶜᶜ? More explicitly, does there exist a family S=(S_n) of total two-party search relations on n input bits, for even n≥2, that has SoML protocols of cost at most C(log₂(2n))^a for some fixed C,a>0, but has no such polylogarithmic PPA protocol bound? For non-membership, the requirement is that for every C′,a′>0 and every N there is an even n≥N for which every correct PPA protocol for S_n costs more than C′(log₂(2n))^{a′}. The graph protocols and their costs are defined below; these are communication classes, not the ordinary Turing-machine or query versions of SoML and PPA.',
 definitions='For each even n, Alice receives x∈{0,1}^{n/2}, Bob receives y∈{0,1}^{n/2}, and S_n⊆{0,1}^{n/2}×{0,1}^{n/2}×O_n, where O_n is a finite output set. Totality means S_n(x,y)={o:(x,y,o)∈S_n} is nonempty for every pair x,y. A local protocol Π_v is a finite deterministic two-party communication tree: each internal node specifies one party, whose transmitted bit depends on its input and the preceding transcript; a leaf has a publicly specified output. Its cost |Π_v| is the maximum number of transmitted bits on any input pair. Local computation and protocol-description size have no resource bound. All protocol data may depend on n, but are fixed before x,y are supplied. No randomization or error is allowed. For either class, choose a nonempty finite vertex set V, a distinguished vertex v*∈V, a fixed label o_v∈O_n for each vertex v, and local protocols Π_v. In particular o_v does not depend on x,y. The cost of this whole graph protocol is ⌈log₂|V|⌉+max_{v∈V}|Π_v|. SoML protocol: Π_v outputs (s_v(x,y),p_v(x,y),ℓ_v(x,y))∈V×V×ℤ. For each input pair form the directed graph with an edge v→u precisely when s_v=u, p_u=v and ℓ_v>ℓ_u. There are no self-loops, in-degree and out-degree are at most one, and the strict decrease makes the graph acyclic. A sink has out-degree zero and a source has in-degree zero; an isolated vertex is both. Correctness requires o_{v*}∈S_n(x,y) whenever v* is a sink or is not a source, and o_v∈S_n(x,y) for every other sink v≠v*. Other sources do not have to label valid answers. Integer meters have no prescribed increment or numerical range; each is the public output of a finite protocol leaf, exactly as in the source. PPA protocol: Π_v outputs a set N_v(x,y)⊆V of at most two candidate neighbors. Form a simple undirected graph with an edge between distinct v,u precisely when u∈N_v and v∈N_u. Nonreciprocal suggestions and self-suggestions create no edge. Correctness requires o_{v*}∈S_n(x,y) if deg(v*)≠1, and o_v∈S_n(x,y) for every v≠v* with deg(v)≠2. In particular an isolated vertex other than v* is a valid witness in this source convention; it must not be silently excluded in favor of an odd-degree-only rule. These conditions guarantee a valid witness for every input: the metered directed graph has a suitable sink, and the undirected parity condition has another endpoint unless the distinguished vertex itself qualifies. The abstract cost charges the vertex-name length and the largest local protocol cost. It does not charge for repeatedly evaluating protocols until a witness is found; asserting membership therefore does not assert a deterministic polylogarithmic communication algorithm that finds the witness directly. Let SoMLᶜᶜ(S_n) and PPAᶜᶜ(S_n) denote the minimum costs of the respective correct graph protocols. A family belongs to a class when that cost is O((log n)^b) for some fixed b, with constants uniform across n. Protocols are nonuniform across input lengths. The requested separation imposes no additional polynomial-time construction requirement on S or the protocols; all the stated relations and correctness claims must nevertheless be mathematically specified.',
 question_type='yes_no',
 answer_criterion='Exhibit and prove the properties of a total search-relation family with polylogarithmic SoML protocol cost and PPA protocol cost outside every polylogarithmic bound, or refute the separation by proving SoMLᶜᶜ⊆PPAᶜᶜ. The non-containment direction must be the one stated. A query-complexity or oracle separation, a lower bound only for deterministic protocols that directly find an answer, or a separation involving the larger class PPADSᶜᶜ alone does not settle this target.',
 context_blocks=[dict(title='Metered paths versus parity witnesses',text='SoML protocols encode a directed collection of paths with a decreasing integer meter and require a sink witness. PPA protocols encode a bounded-degree undirected graph and use its endpoint structure. The question asks whether efficient local communication descriptions based on the first principle can always be replaced by descriptions based on the second.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The source separates a larger class',text='The paper proves PPADSᶜᶜ⊈PPAᶜᶜ. SoML adds a decreasing meter to the directed witness structure, so the existing PPADS separation does not automatically place a hard relation in SoML.',citation='primary'),dict(title='Connections to monotone computation',text='The source characterizes PPA communication complexity using monotone span programs over the two-element field. It shows that monotone comparator circuits give SoML protocols, but does not establish a converse characterization. The class separation is therefore related to, rather than stated as equivalent to, a comparator-circuit versus span-program separation.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The question is repeated in a later survey',text='The 2022 survey explicitly asks again for SoMLᶜᶜ⊈PPAᶜᶜ while describing remaining gaps in communication versions of total search classes.',citation='survey'),dict(title='A query separation does not settle the communication question',text='The 2024 JACM paper proves a corresponding separation for the query class SOPL against PPA, yielding an oracle separation for ordinary computation. Its discussion explicitly asks for communication analogues of its results. The superscript indicating the computational model is essential.',citation='query')],
 why='Would separate two basic finite-graph existence principles when inputs are split between communicating parties, refining the connection between total search complexity and monotone algebraic computation.',
 references=refs,progress=[dict(date='2019',text='PPADSᶜᶜ is separated from PPAᶜᶜ; the stronger placement of a hard problem in SoMLᶜᶜ is posed as open.',citation='primary'),dict(date='2022',text='The survey repeats the precise communication-class separation question.',citation='survey'),dict(date='2024',text='The journal paper proves SOPLᵈᵗ⊈PPAᵈᵗ and expressly asks about communication analogues; it is not recorded as a resolution of this card.',citation='query')],
 status='open',status_note='Read the source appendix and full ECCC definitions, the 2022 survey question, and the 2024 JACM query/oracle theorem and remaining-question paragraph. Checked subsequent-work searches through 12 September 2026, including the separate 2024 TFNP intersection/collapse results. No communication-class resolution was located. Searches are not exhaustive; no lifting argument or paper proof was independently verified.',model_self_contained=True,requires_context=False,
 review_note='Uses exactly the source’s graph-protocol model and endpoint exceptions. SoML is a named protocol class here; ordinary polynomial-time search, deterministic communication search cost and query complexity are not substituted for it.',
 importance=dict(score=c['importance']['score'],method='editorial',reason='Tests the relative strength of metered-path and parity-based total search in communication complexity, with a concrete connection to monotone comparator and span-program models. Existing score retained.',assessed_on=DATE),
 working_summary=dict(sentences=['SoML and PPA communication protocols describe different implicit graphs through low-cost local two-party protocols.','SoML requires sink witnesses on directed paths with a decreasing meter, while PPA requires endpoint or exceptional-degree witnesses in undirected graphs.','The question asks for a relation with polylogarithmic SoML cost but no polylogarithmic PPA cost.','The source’s separation for the larger PPADS class and its comparator-circuit connection do not establish this claim.','A 2024 query/oracle separation is known, but that paper explicitly leaves communication analogues for further work.'],basis='saved_sources',source_basis='source-text',written_on=DATE,source_refs=['primary','full','survey','query'])
),notes=notes,checked_sources=[r['url'] for r in refs]+['https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02168','https://doi.org/10.1137/22M1498346'])
